le":"Mark Graduation with the Senior Class Gift","subtitle":"A giving tradition tied to a philanthropy cord","notes":"Graduating seniors can review the current campaign before contributing; confirm the stated minimum and cord eligibility for the active class year.","short_summary":"Seniors begin their alumni relationship through a class-year donation supporting Hofstra's educational work.","evidence_claim":"Hofstra describes the Senior Class Gift as an enduring tradition supporting undergraduate education; the Class of 2026 minimum gift was $20.26 and qualified donors for a philanthropy cord.","source_url":"https://www.hofstra.edu/alumni/senior-class-gift/","source_title":"Senior Class Gift","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Intended for graduating seniors; contribution thresholds and cord eligibility are class-year specific and should be checked before giving.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"hofstra-walk-of-pride","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Walk of Pride","title":"Find Hofstra Stories Engraved in the Walk of Pride","subtitle":"Named bricks beside Shuart Stadium and Alumni House","notes":"Read the engraved names in Stadium Plaza, or consult Alumni Affairs before ordering a commemorative brick for a student, graduate, or friend.","short_summary":"Hofstra supporters leave permanent engraved names in a brick pathway connecting campus memory and philanthropy.","evidence_claim":"Hofstra identifies the Walk of Pride as a special tradition composed of bricks engraved with students', alumni's, and friends' names in Stadium Plaza.","source_url":"https://www.hofstra.edu/alumni/fund/","source_title":"The Fund for Hofstra University: Alumni and Development","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,